        -- consume one token matching `expected` (string or set); produces
        -- no capture (returning only the new position) so token strings
        -- never leak into the surrounding rule's capture stream.  The
        -- inner P(1) is a single-byte dummy so LPeg's verifier sees a
        -- consuming pattern (Cmt(P(true)) would look potentially-empty
        -- and trigger a false left-recursion warning through
        -- base -> choice -> term -> factor -> base); the callback looks
        -- the token up at pos-1 and jumps to the end of the whole token,
        -- which may be a multi-byte cluster
